    "body": "# Issues\r\n\r\nSteps to reproduce:\r\n1. Create a task that does something insignificant (for .e.g sleeps for 5 mins)\r\n2. Configure the task with max_retry=3 times. Start the worker and the task.\r\n3. Find the task pid and send SIGKILL to it. Notice that the task is restarted immediately\r\n4. Repeat this 5 or more times and notice that the task is restarted immediately every time even after the the number of retries exceeds the configured max_retry.\r\n\r\nIn production the process could be killed because the task ran out of memory and the kernel OOM selected to kill it.\r\n\r\nThis could also be automated by having a task that simply performs suicide using something like this: os.kill(os.getpid(), signal.SIGKILL).\r\n\r\nI would expect the max_retry and other options from the Retires middleware to also work if the task process is terminated abruptly.\r\n\r\n## What OS are you using?\r\n\r\nUsing Linux, Ubuntu 18.04.\r\n\r\n## What version of Dramatiq are you using?\r\n\r\ndramatiq 1.6.0\r\n\r\n",
